=EF=BB=BFOn 2023-01-07, 18:13, "Stephen Farrell" <stephen.farrell@cs.tcd.ie=
> wrote:=0D=0D=0D>Hiya, =0D> =0D>On 07/01/2023 15:46, John Mattsson wrote: =
=0D>> My current understanding is that draft-ietf-tls-esni should require =
=0D>> that the server MUST NOT reuse a key shares. Unless I miss something =
=0D>> I suggest adding that and one or two of the above figures to the =0D>=
> draft. An alternative solution would be to extend the ECH encryption =0D>=
> to also cover ServerHello. If I understand ECH correctly, the =0D>> Serve=
rHello is still unencrypted. =0D> =0D>I'd support adding a requirement that=
 key shares not be =0D>re-used, either as a general thing or in an ECH-spec=
ific =0D>manner. =0D=0DI made an issue and PR for RFC8446bis. For privacy r=
easons, I think this should be SHOULD NOT as a general thing. For servers u=
sing ECH, I think MUST NOT seems motivated. Does MUST NOT lead to DoS probl=
ems for servers using x25519? =0D=0Dhttps://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/iss=
ues/1285 <https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/issues/1285> =0Dhttps://githu=
b.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1286 <https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/=
1286> =0D=0DCheers, =0DJohn =0D=0D=0D=

--_42B80531-508D-EB4B-9169-E4808A6FED85_
